stranger things season 4 to me is the  best season since the first given that  season 2 had a couple rough patches and  season 3 was fun despite the writing  being a bit ridiculous at times with  season 4 The Duffer brothers gave  themselves an extra year to work on the  season and I think the quality really  shows through the final product we have  a gripping narrative that not only so  introduces a lot of new interesting  developments but also delves deep into  the lore and gives us a lot of answers  to questions that have been burning a  hole in us for years Revelations like  one actually being vechna the lab  Massacre not being caused by 11. and  vechna being the one that creates the  Mind flare and the overall essence of  The Upside Down are all excellent  directions to take the story the overall  concept of The Upside Down is so rich  and intriguing that we as an audience  have been craving for some backstory for  the upside down and the fact that the  Duffer Brothers not only deliver on that  but exceed it is impressive this reminds  me of Game of Thrones season 8 where  fans were clamoring for some backstory  for the white walkers but were  ultimately denied and the writers said  nothing with it but here for stranger  things it's a breath of fresh air to  feel more than satisfied with the  writing of the show and it hasn't gone  down in quality over the years then on  the subject of over the years the acting  is at its best from will still  delivering scenes with extreme emotional  depth characters like Lucas and Dustin  who haven't had a lot of deep material  to work with prior who managed to rise  to the occasion especially Dustin with  that heartbreaking final scene where he  tells Eddie's father that he died and  characters like 11 still proving that  there are magnificent highlights and  this isn't even mentioning the standout  performance of the season with  sadistan's portrayal of Max the way she  showcases the sheer complexity of  feeling grief regrets and overall having  so many feelings chipping away at our  mental well-being is crazily impressive  then this is also tied into her  character having a spectacular Arc of  escaping vecta and then even going back  to face him again despite what she's  been through she really steals the show  this season for the Hawkins storyline  where the death Brothers do with it is  completely riveting from the creepy and  shocking horror of people getting  crumpled up like paper throwing our  characters down a deep Rabbit Hole of an  intriguing mystery the Striking  Revelations that are brought about by  crazy twists and there's even some great  and original action like with Eddie  ripping a guitar solo to lure in bats  there's really no down moments during  the entire stretch of time in Hawkins  and it makes the other plot lines like  with Mike and Company and Hopper being  stuck in Russia feel a bit less in  comparison which this also leads into a  couple small gripes I have in season 4  because currently every character within  Hawkins is perfectly utilized and fills  a specific function that has a men's  purpose but when you look at the pizza  van Adventure Mike Will and Jonathan  fall into the backgrounds and more so  Jonathan because he essentially just  turns into a taxi driver this season and  this is inherently just where the  characters are left off because being so  far away from Hawkins and separated from  11 doesn't really give these guys much  to do then to even Compound on this  feeling of disconnection Jim Hopper for  being in a Russian prison doesn't feel  like it fits well into the story  especially since how does him going  through a portal on Hawkins teleport him  to Russia wouldn't he just end up in the  upside down version of the mall or did  he not actually go through the portal  and was captured in Hawkins which also  wouldn't make sense because the EOS Army  was surrounding the mall currently it  feels like they left us intentionally  vague because they know this development  is illogical but would have gave Hopper  more of a purpose within the season  would be for his character to instead be  trapped in the upside down by going  through the portal at the end of season  3 and is then captured by vechna to then  be utilized as a hostage to manipulate  11. I know this is a drastically  different idea than having hopper in  Russia but the alternative is having a  crazy and ridiculous plot for Joyce and  Murray to go to Russia and break Hopper  out of prison that aspect is just as  absurd as in season 3 where there's an  entire underground Russian base in  Hawkins and kids are able to infiltrate  it like breaking in and out of this  really scary prison was far too easy  then the The Duffer Brothers try to  infuse this plotline with some Purpose  By the Russians capturing part of the  Mind flayer which I have no idea how  they manage that given that it's a  gaseous entity and it seems like it's  only there so that the good guys can  destroy it to help everyone back in  Hawkins which they conveniently kill it  when everyone in the upside down is  about to die so as it stands this feels  like a bit of a contrived way to give  Hopper's plotline more purpose but I  feel like this won't be as much of an  issue in season 5 because everyone is  back in Hawkins again and the connection  will probably be much stronger between  every character then from another small  issue is that the season felt a bit  bloated given that there were like six  to seven active subplots going at a time  in some aspects of those plot lines  didn't feel very essential for the story  one of those being L getting bullied at  school for an extended period of time  for this whole development there's not  much of an impact on the plot since L  just gets plucked out of confinement and  was sent to training not to mention that  this bullying development felt a bit  redundant since they did it again in  11's training flashback this isn't a  major issue and there's one clever thing  that The Duffer Brothers do to alleviate  this problem of juggling so many  subplots which is the usage of parallel  editing and for people who don't know  parallel editing is separate scenes  intercut together to present a storyline  for multiple perspectives an example of  this is Robert and Nancy interviewing  Henry's father while Max is being  pursued by vecna or in the first episode  where the DND matches playing out during  Lucas's basketball game this energizes  the pace of the show and what makes  these intricate scenes even better is  the editing because to me a well-placed  match cut is pure dopamine for my brain  because of how clever it is but overall  by using parallel editing it Bridges the  gap between so many subplots and allows  the writers to tell stories  simultaneously on top of presenting  these scenes in a much more creative  manner so all these subplots never  really feel like a burden because of how  well paced they are and their coherent  Synergy throughout the episode going  back to the Hawkins plotline there's one  more aspect I want to talk about in the  season that elevates it over the others  which is the r of danger that surrounds  everyone since 11 isn't in Hawkins to  protect our beloved characters makes a  stake significantly higher because they  can't hide behind the leaven anymore  this was as well the same case with  season 2 which I think also did a great  job with having higher Stakes but that  only lasts an episode and a half since  11 comes back from a brief vacation and  things don't start getting dicey towards  the end of the season that feeling of  helplessness and having to overcome a  seemingly impossible task is applied to  the entirety of season four because the  threat starts much sooner along with the  fact of our characters having to figure  out the mystery by themselves this kind  of writing where you can't point to a  clear and easy solution and puzzles the  audience until being wowed by the answer  is to me my favorite aspect of writing  and The Duffer Brothers managed to do  this in almost every episode that's why  the scene where our characters cleverly  outsmarting vechna where Max escapes  using music she loves was one of the  best scenes in the show it's immensely  satisfying on top of the execution in  season 4 being epic as well then going  back to the higher Stakes it immerses  every scene with so much tension because  at any point one of our characters could  die even early on when Steve gets  dragged down into the upside down by  himself and gets ravaged by bats you  question his safety I know he probably  won't ever die but there was definitely  a moment there where he questioned  whether or not he would survive that  situation which that's great although  it's kind of miraculous that the bites  from the bats didn't have any alien  diseases but whatever I don't want to  think about that because Steve is the  best character in the show and he's  A-Okay he just might give Nancy alien  AIDS in season five I'm sure that's  exactly what people would want overall I  think the season exudes such a high  quality and it's surprising to me that  stranger things has about the same  budget of Obi-Wan per episode but  stranger things has both a much better  production value and is significantly  longer this allows for The Duffer  Brothers to do a deep dive with their  writing despite some of the subplots  feeling a bit disconnected with a lack  of unifying purpose but now that  everyone is together for season five I'm  sure the Duffer Brothers will come up  with a better way to utilize every  character more efficiently and since  there will be an apocalypse of sorts I  doubt 11 will be able to protect  everyone so that are of danger probably  won't evaporate thank you for watching  and let me know what you think about  season 4 in the comments
 

